            "review_title": "Review at Square Cafe",
            "review_text": "alexknows777\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nSquare Cafe- A nice place to get away from the hustle and bustle of the city.\nOct 2011\nIt is a really clean place that has a smoking section on the second and fourth floor, which is a delight for non-smokers trying to escape the smoker friendly reputation of the city. It’s a very chilled out modern place, with creative designs that are very inviting. \n\nThe staff all speak English and are really friendly. They all are very helpful, suggesting wonderful dishes to try. Even though it’s a cafe, it has its standard fare of Western and Vietnamese dishes at reasonable prices. I had the spaghetti carbonnara which tasted quite good, and the strawberry smoothies were awesome. \n\nThe cafe is a wonderful place to hangout and relax, a great get away from constant noise of the city. It has such a beautiful view of the Opera House and the surrounding gardens. I would visit here again on my next trip to Hanoi.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 14, 2011",
